.TH FL-PACKAGES 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-packages \- Software Packages: packages and updates for fldesktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-packages\fR [\fB\-\-updates\fR | \fB\-\-search\fR \fITERM\fR |
\fB\-\-show\fR \fINAME\fR [\fB\-\-tab\fR \fBfiles\fR|\fBdepends\fR|\fBrequired-by\fR]]
.br
\fBfl-packages\fR \fIFILE\fR...
.br
\fBfl-packages \-\-check\-updates\fR [\fB\-\-now\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manages the system's software through PackageKit, so it works with the
package manager of the distribution (apt, pacman, dnf, zypper...):
.TP
\fBUpdates\fR
lists the available updates (security updates first), shows their
description, changelog and security advisories, and installs the checked
ones. \fBCheck Now\fR refreshes the package lists.
.TP
\fBSoftware\fR
searches packages by name or description, browses them by group or lists
the installed ones, shows details and installs or removes them. The
\fBFiles\fR tab lists the files of a package, \fBDepends on\fR the packages
it needs and \fBRequired by\fR the installed packages that need it
(directly, or also indirectly); a double click shows that package.
.TP
\fBRepositories\fR
enables and disables software sources.
.TP
\fBHistory\fR
shows the changes made through PackageKit.
.PP
Before a change fl-packages asks PackageKit what else it involves
(dependencies to install, packages to remove) and lists it for
confirmation. Packages without a trusted signature are only installed
after a second question. Administrator rights are asked for by
\fBfl-polkit-agent\fR(1).
.PP
Given package files (.deb, .rpm, .pkg.tar.zst...), fl-packages installs
them.
.SH UPDATE CHECKS
\fBfl-packages \-\-check\-updates\fR is started at login
(\fI/etc/xdg/autostart/fl-packages-updates.desktop\fR). A minute later (at
once with \fB\-\-now\fR), and then every six hours, it refreshes the package
lists when they are older than the configured interval and sends a
notification when updates are available; the notification opens the
Updates tab. The same updates are announced only once. Between checks it
only sleeps: each check runs as \fBfl-packages \-\-check\-updates
\-\-once\fR, which does one check and ends.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/fldesktop/updates.ini\fR
[Updates] Check=hourly|daily|weekly|never, Notify=true|false (the Software
Updates page of \fBfl-settings\fR(1)).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpkcon\fR(1), \fBfl-flatpak\fR(1), \fBfl-settings\fR(1)
